  "id": "predictive-efficiency",
  "term": "predictive efficiency",
  "definition": "Predictive efficiency is how well a prediction model can correctly distinguish between people who will and will not have a particular outcome. In this context, it refers to the model’s overall effectiveness as shown by performance measures such as discrimination, sensitivity, and specificity.",
